      {
        "id": 229172,
        "name": "aramis",
        "username": "aramis",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/aramis/{size}/1871_2.png",
        "created_at": "2019-12-03T22:36:46.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Powerhound_2000\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/powerhound_2000/48/1859_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Powerhound_2000:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I disagree it works that way based off what you posted.  However, I agree it does work that way off the wording I see looking again in most recent version of chapter 3</p>\n<div>Quote:<br>\n<blockquote>\n<p>When an opponent would deal you damage, you may roll your single [power] die as a Defend and also redirect that damage to a nearby target, other than the source of the Attack.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</div>\n<p>Based off this wording you redirect the whole damage to another target and you have an active Defend that lasts until your turn.  So with that I’m retracting my comment in the playtesting forum as it seems clear to me with that wording.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Let me formulaically show what that looks like to me:<br>\nT = X - R<br>\nY = R<br>\nIncoming damage  X<br>\nOutgoing damage  Y<br>\nTaken damage T<br>\nRolled deflect R</p>\n<p>It’s still fuzzy, I’d rather see a wording like:<br>\nWhen taking damage, roll your single power die ones, using it both as  a defend against the attack and as a counter-attack against the one who had attacked you.</p>",
        "post_number": 32,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:03:51.272Z",
